error[ambiguous-concat]: `[1 -2]` concatenates `-2` as new element
 --> positive.jl:2:7
  |
2 | row = [1 -2]
  |       ^^^^^^ 1×2 matrix
  |          -- separate element
  |
  = why: space before sign starts new element; `1 - 2` would subtract
  = confidence: possible
  = fix: write `[1, -2]` for vector, `[1 - 2]` for arithmetic   [manual]
  = docs: corset explain ambiguous-concat
  = note: deny from correctness group, library preset

error[ambiguous-concat]: `[x -y]` concatenates `-y` as new element
 --> positive.jl:3:8
  |
3 | pair = [x -y]
  |        ^^^^^^ 1×2 matrix
  |           -- separate element
  |
  = why: space before sign starts new element; `x - y` would subtract
  = confidence: possible
  = fix: write `[x, -y]` for vector, `[x - y]` for arithmetic   [manual]
  = docs: corset explain ambiguous-concat

